{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). mark, feeling rejected and angry, creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and attracts the attention of the harvard administration.\n\nmark is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), two rowers who are also students at harvard, with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work with the winklevoss twins, but eventually drops the project and starts working on his own version of the site, which he calls \"thefacebook\".\n\nmark teams up with his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), and together they launch thefacebook, which quickly becomes a huge success. however, the winklevoss twins claim that mark stole their idea and sue him for intellectual property theft.\n\nthe movie follows the subsequent lawsuits and the rise of facebook as a global phenomenon. the film also explores the personal relationships between mark, eduardo, and the winklevoss twins, and how they are affected by the success of facebook.\n\nthe social network features excellent performances from its cast, particularly jesse eisenberg and andrew garfield. the film's script is also noteworthy, with aaron sorkin's witty dialogue and clever character development. the movie's cinematography is also impressive, with a dark and moody tone that captures the intensity and competitiveness of the harvard university environment.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its ability to balance the technical aspects of facebook's creation with the personal relationships and conflicts between the characters. the film also raises important questions about the nature of friendship, loyalty, and the consequences of success.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted and engaging film that provides a fascinating look at the creation of facebook and the people behind it. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the history of social media and the impact it has had on our lives.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24996495246887207}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05464606732130051}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.18567566573619843}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -9.298368240706623e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.218656047465629e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.017032857984304428}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015200339839793742}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00016094549209810793}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08091060072183609}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.11775506287813187}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017488384619355202}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0036843856796622276}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00590532785281539}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.06923678517341614}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0008205560734495521}, {